### The first real tick — and the bug it caught (2026-08-06)
- [x] **`WORKERS_ENABLED=true` set on Railway `staging`** (environment verified by
      `RAILWAY_ENVIRONMENT_NAME`/`SENTRY_ENVIRONMENT` before writing — the CLI was linked to
      **production** by default, which is one typo away from starting rent generation on live data).
      Boot markers confirmed: `workers ENABLED (4 workers + dispatch)` + `schedulers registered`.
- [x] **Fired a tick by hand rather than waiting for the cron.** Next natural tick was ~21 hours
      out (00:30 Asia/Karachi). Enqueued the same job the scheduler writes, via the Redis public
      proxy URL.
- [x] **It failed — and the failure was real code, not the harness.** `Custom Id cannot contain :`.
      BullMQ accepts a custom job ID with ':' only when it splits into exactly three parts, so
      `rent:<hostelId>:<month>` passed by luck and `auto-cancel:<day>` threw. **The nightly sweep
      would have failed at 00:30 tonight and every night after** — no beds freed, which is the
      exact defect the producer work exists to close. Fixed in `3fb5a6e`: `lib/job-ids.ts` owns ID
      construction, `-` separator, throws on ':' and on all-integer IDs.
- [x] **DLQ proven end to end on staging** — the failed tick landed in `dlq_jobs` with its error
      message. First time that path has run outside CI.
- [x] **Re-fired after `3fb5a6e` deployed — full chain green.** `[dispatch] enqueued global sweep`
      → `[auto-cancel] Running job auto-cancel-2026-08-05` → `No cancellations due` → `completed`.
      The no-op is honest: staging has no cancellation with a passed vacate date.
- [x] **`rent-monthly` fired — the money path has now run.** `enqueued 1 hostels` →
      `3 created, 0 skipped`. Rows verified in the DB: rent mirrors `monthly_fee` (8000/8000/9500),
      `admission_fee` and `concession` 0, `total_due` = `unpaid`, status `pending`, receipts 1–3.
- [x] **Idempotency proven, not assumed.** Fired rent a second time: `rent-generate` completed
      count unchanged and August still has exactly 3 rows — the deterministic job ID
      (`rent-<hostelId>-2026-08`) was refused by BullMQ as a duplicate. This is the guard that lets
      every replica run the dispatcher without billing a hostel N times.
- [x] **`rent-generate` now bills `mess_fee` — FIXED `3b432c1`, CI green (run 31053240161).**
      It inserted `rent = monthly_fee` and ignored the column, while migration 014 calls it "billed
      together with monthly_fee". Unnoticed on staging because all 3 students have `mess_fee NULL`;
      the first student with a mess fee would have been under-billed every month.
      **Billed as a `payment_extra_charges` row, not folded into `rent`** — the canonical formula is
      `rent + admission_fee + Σ(extras) - concession` and `PATCH /payments/:id` recalculates from
      the real extras rows, so a total carrying mess with no row behind it would be silently
      reduced by the first owner edit. NULL still gets no line; 0.00 gets a zero line (014's
      "included, zero-rated"). Payment + mess line share one transaction via the new `lib/tx.ts`
      (extracted from billing-sync, now used by both). Money arithmetic moved into Postgres —
      `8000.00 + 0.10` is not 8000.10 in a double (INVARIANT-4).
      4 DB-backed tests; the load-bearing one recomputes the canonical formula from what is on disk
      so the generator and the PATCH recalc cannot drift.
- [ ] **Not yet proven against a real mess student on staging.** All 3 staging students have
      `mess_fee NULL`, so the fix is proven by CI against a seeded DB, not by a live tick. To close
      it: set a `mess_fee` on one staging student, fire `rent-monthly` for a fresh month, confirm
      the extra-charge row. The 3 existing August rows were written by the old code and need no
      backfill — those students genuinely have no mess.
- [ ] ⚠️ **`WORKERS_ENABLED` is still OFF in production, and must stay off** until both of the
      above are green on staging.

