## ★ SESSION 16 — THE WORKERS FINALLY HAVE A PRODUCER (2026-08-06)
> Closes the P0 from `docs/_audit-2026-07-30`: `apps/api` had four `Worker`s and zero `Queue`s,
> so rent was never generated, pending cancellations were never confirmed (beds stayed occupied)
> and trials never expired. Committed `d205b8f` (billing-sync) + `726b77d` (producers).
- [x] **`lib/queues.ts`** — four queues, shared retry/retention, deterministic job IDs.
- [x] **`workers/dispatch.ts`** — tick + fan-out scheduler. Rent 00:00 on the 1st, auto-cancel
      00:30 daily, trial sweep 02:00 daily, all Asia/Karachi. A tick re-reads the tenant list every
      run, so it cannot drift when a hostel signs up or churns.
- [x] **`WORKERS_ENABLED` flag (default OFF)** in `server.ts` + `.env.example`. Dynamic imports —
      the worker modules construct their `Worker` at module scope, so a static import would start
      them regardless of the flag.
- [x] **`billing-sync` was unrunnable** — fake transactions (`pool.query('BEGIN')` across pooled
      connections), `hostels` addressed by a non-existent `hostel_id`, three status values no CHECK
      constraint permits ('expired', 'archived', 'trialing'), and a write to a non-existent
      `subscriptions.suspended_at`. All fixed; trial expiry now lands on 'suspended'.
- [x] **`queues.test.ts`** — producer/worker parity + "every `.add()` passes a jobId" + "pii_purge
      is not scheduled", as static source assertions so they run without Redis on every push. 4/4.
- [x] `tsc --noEmit` clean · `eslint src` clean.

