## ★ SESSION 10 — PHASE 2 STARTED: apps/web scaffolded (2026-07-27, PR #35)
- [x] **`apps/web` exists and works end-to-end against the live staging API** — Next.js 16 App
      Router, TypeScript strict, in the pnpm workspace + turbo (lint/build/typecheck all wired).
      Verified by running the built app against staging: middleware redirects, login through the
      proxy, and the dashboard + students screens rendering real seeded data.
- [x] **Auth is a server-side proxy, deliberately.** The browser never calls the API directly.
      Reason: the API's refresh cookie is `sameSite: 'strict'` + `path=/api/v1/auth/refresh`, and
      Vercel↔Railway are *different sites*, so a browser would never send it — every session would
      have died at the 15-minute access-token expiry with no obvious cause. Refreshing server-side
      avoids it and keeps working once app./api.hostyllo.app make them same-site. Tokens also never
      touch client JS (httpOnly cookies this app owns).
- [x] **Design tokens transcribed verbatim** from `docs/04_UX_DESIGN_SYSTEM.md` §2 into
      `src/app/tokens.css` (dark default). 44px touch targets, 16px inputs (no iOS zoom), inline
      errors not alerts, zoom left enabled — per that doc's warden-on-a-cheap-Android brief.
- [x] **Screens:** login, dashboard (6 KPIs + needs-attention), students (search + pagination),
      **payments** (month/status filters + month summary strip, voided rows dimmed) and **rooms**
      (bed-occupancy grid — the "where can I put someone" view, per blueprint Module 3). PR #36.
- [x] **Shared list primitives** extracted to a single shared `ui` module once there were three list
      screens (table frame, notice, pagination that carries filters forward, status badge, stat
      grid). Dashboard and students refactored onto them in the same pass.
      **Superseded in session 11** — that file is deleted; its pieces now live in
      `apps/web/src/components/patterns/` and the restyled `ui-kit`.
- [x] **Next.js 16, not 14** as the docs specify. Deliberate: scaffolding a new app on an older
      major right after fixing the Fastify EOL would repeat the mistake. Note Next 16 removed the
      `eslint` config key — linting is a separate CI step.

### 🐞 BUG FOUND BY BUILDING THE FRONTEND — FIXED (PR #35)
- [x] **`POST /students` never marked the assigned bed occupied.** `beds.status` was only ever
      written by `/rooms/shift` and cancellation-restore, so every student added through the normal
      flow left their bed `'vacant'`. Double-booking was still prevented (that check reads the
      students table), but **the dashboard and `/rooms` both derive occupancy from `beds.status`,
      so a full hostel reported 0%**. Found by rendering the real dashboard, not by any test.
      Fixed on create + released on soft-delete, with a regression test.
- [ ] ⚠️ **Related, NOT fixed:** `PATCH /students/:id` can change `bed_id` without moving
      `beds.status`. `/rooms/shift` is the intended path for moves; decide whether PATCH should
      reject a `bed_id` change or maintain the status itself.
- [x] ⚠️ **API returns money as strings — FIXED 2026-07-28 (session 12), at the driver.**
      Was `revenuePkr: "11000.00"`, `activeStudents: "3"`; pg returns NUMERIC (oid 1700) and INT8
      (oid 20, what COUNT() returns) as strings. Fixed with `pg.types.setTypeParser` for both in
      `packages/db/src/withTenant.ts` — the one module that creates the pools, so it covers every
      route and worker at once.
      **Why there and not in `dashboard.ts`:** this is the *fourth* instance of one defect. The
      rent string-concat bug, the 10× rent-generate bug, and these responses were each fixed by
      adding one more hand-written `Number()` at one more call site, which holds only until
      someone forgets — and forgetting is silent, since `"5000" + "1000"` is legal JavaScript.
      Parsing at the driver ends the class; the existing `Number()`/`parseInt()` calls in the
      routes become harmless no-ops rather than load-bearing.
      INT8 is parsed defensively (keeps the string if it would not survive the round trip, so an
      unrepresentable value fails loudly instead of arriving quietly wrong). NUMERIC deliberately
      has no such guard: money that overflowed a double is far outside `NUMERIC(10,2)`, and
      returning a string there would resurrect the concatenation bug being removed.
      Guarded by `numeric-types.test.ts` (4 tests) over dashboard stats, defaulters and the
      payments list, including one that asserts the figures *add* rather than concatenate. Two
      now-false `amount: string` annotations in `payments.ts` corrected.

