      28/28 FORCE RLS, /health green.
- [x] **🔴 Fastify 4 EOL → UPGRADED to 5.10.0** (PR #31, 2026-07-27). Plugins: cors 11, helmet 13,
      cookie 11, multipart 10 (retires the v10→v8 downgrade). Only code change: Fastify 5 widened
      `setErrorHandler`'s error param to `unknown` → annotated `FastifyError`. `fast-uri >=3.1.4`
      `engines.node: >=20` added (Railway picks its own runtime). **Audit 42 → 28 findings,
      criticals 5 → 2**; the fastify/find-my-way advisories are gone and the rest is dev
      (vitest/vite/postcss) or build-time (tar, brace-expansion via bcrypt node-pre-gyp).
- [ ] **fast-uri override still owed** — Fastify 5.10.0 resolves `fast-uri` 3.1.2 transitively via
      ajv/the fastify compilers; needs ≥3.1.4 (host confusion). Fix is a pnpm `overrides` entry,
      but it must live in `pnpm-workspace.yaml` (pnpm 10+ stopped reading `pnpm.overrides` from
      package.json) and be written to the lockfile BY pnpm 11 — CI fails
      `ERR_PNPM_LOCKFILE_CONFIG_MISMATCH` otherwise. Blocked on the dev-env drift below.
      **This drift has now cost three CI cycles** (overrides location, engines.node runtime pick,
      and `allowBuilds` for sharp) — each passed locally on pnpm 9 and failed on CI's pnpm 11.
- [x] **`engines.node` broke the staging deploy — FIXED (PR #32).** The Fastify 5 merge failed to
      deploy: Railway's railpack **reads `engines.node` to CHOOSE the runtime**, so the `">=20"`
      added for Fastify 5 made it install Node **20.20.2** — and pnpm 11.1.1 (from
      `packageManager`) needs ≥22.13, so `pnpm install` died with
      `ERR_UNKNOWN_BUILTIN_MODULE: node:sqlite`. Before that field existed railpack defaulted to a
      newer Node, so a *loose lower bound pinned the build to the oldest allowed version*. Now
      `">=22.13"` — the real floor, set by pnpm 11, and what CI already runs. Prod was unaffected
      (deploys from `main`); staging kept serving the previous good build.
- [ ] **Dev-env drift** — repo declares `packageManager: pnpm@11.1.1`; the dev machine runs pnpm
      9.15.9 on Node 20.19.2, and pnpm 11 refuses to start on Node 20
      (`ERR_UNKNOWN_BUILTIN_MODULE`). CI runs pnpm 11 / Node 22. Anything touching overrides or
      lockfile config passes locally and fails in CI. Install Node 22 locally (nvm) and use
      corepack, or pin CI's pnpm to the version this machine can actually run.
- [ ] 🟡 Unknown routes return Fastify's default 404 body, not the `{success,code,message}`
      envelope every other response uses (`code` is undefined). Add `setNotFoundHandler` before
      the Phase-2 frontend starts consuming error shapes. Found during the Fastify 5 smoke test;
      deliberately kept out of the upgrade PR to keep that diff reviewable.
- [x] **🟠 Authorization matrix — RESOLVED against PRD §4.2 (PR #34).** Drift was worse than the
      audit found: **3 violations**, not 1. chain_manager was denied student read/write (matrix: ✓),
      and *wrongly allowed* payment edit and settings access (matrix: — for both). `viewer` is a
      real read-only role → GET access to operational data, but NOT audit-log or reveal-cnic (a
      security log and a decrypted CNIC are not "reports"). Matrix now lives in one file,
      `apps/api/src/lib/roles.ts`, instead of inlined at 64 call sites — that duplication is why it
      drifted invisibly. `roles.test.ts` asserts it against live responses per role. Zero live
      impact: prod has 2 users, both hostel_owner.
      ⚠️ PRD §4.3 per-warden `can_delete`/`can_settings`/`can_edit` flags remain UNIMPLEMENTED (no
      columns in any migration) — wardens get the role-level answer. Deliberate; wire in roles.ts.
